[cdavey@hpcuhb.HP.COM (Chuck Davey) writes:]
[] This "level-teleport" business has me perplexed ...

follow me, if you don't mind spoilers (lurking ahead!) ...

not all of this is spoilers ...

there are three circumstances in which you can acquire teleport
control:
1) wearing a ring of teleport control (not teleportation).
2) randomly acquiring the intrinsic attribute by eating a tengu
    corpse. when this happens you feel in control of yourself.
3) playing a wizard character and having experience level greater
    than or equal to level 17. you feel controlled when crossing
    this juncture.

the rest of the discussion assumes you have teleport control since
that is needed to control your level teleports, which means you can
select the level you'd like to visit.

there are two basic methods by which you can level teleport:
1) a level teleport trap. these traps occur more frequently the
    lower you explore and also can be found behind secret doors
    which have the smudged engraving "ad aererium" adjacent to
    them. the teleport trap will not affect you if are wearing
    armor which has the magic protection attribute (typically
    a wizard's starting cloak).

2) confusion coupled with scrolls of teleportation. reading a
    cursed scroll of teleportation under normal circumstances
    will level teleport you. additionally, reading a not cursed
    scroll of teleportation while confused will also level
    teleport you.

level teleporting is the only way to reach the deep hell levels! try
a controlled level teleport to level 99 when you're ready to explore
hell. note the level you actually arrive at and then only go that
far in future trips. this will typically be level 50 (nethack 3.0).
in hell don't expect to find down stairwells, there aren't any. there
are down ladders on a few special levels associated with Vlad, however
the ladders will be unaccessible unless you enter "Vlad's towers" from
the deepest/lowest level where the only normal secret door entrance is.
Of course, passing thru walls will get you in there also.

if these features aren't in your dungeon, as described, then something
is amiss. talk to your games administrator!

